Subject: local: allow the conformance emulator in the GitHub read-only profile

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. This is a Breadboard-local substitution, recorded under
decision 3 of the Fullsend integration conformance plan.

A provider profile is the sandbox's network allowlist. Fullsend imports
profiles verbatim and expands no variables in them, which is the right
behaviour for a policy file: an environment variable should not be able to
widen what a sandbox may reach. The consequence is that a host which varies
per environment cannot be templated, and the conformance forge is a GitHub
emulator on a cluster address.

So the emulator's host is added here explicitly. The posture is unchanged:
read-only, enforced, and the binary allowlist still excludes curl so the agent
cannot make raw HTTP calls with the injected token.

If this profile ever becomes templatable upstream, this patch should be dropped
rather than rebased.

Breadboard note: applied to the agents mirror by
deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-agents.py.

diff --git a/profiles/fullsend-github-ro.yaml b/profiles/fullsend-github-ro.yaml
index e3d9545..22821d4 100644
--- a/profiles/fullsend-github-ro.yaml
+++ b/profiles/fullsend-github-ro.yaml
@@ -22,6 +22,27 @@ endpoints:
     protocol: rest
     access: read-only
     enforcement: enforce
+  # Breadboard-local: the conformance forge is a GitHub emulator on a cluster
+  # address, and this profile is the sandbox's network allowlist. Fullsend
+  # imports profiles verbatim and does not expand variables in them, which is
+  # correct for a policy file, so a host that varies per environment can only
+  # be added by editing it. That makes this a local substitution rather than
+  # something to send upstream.
+  #
+  # The read-only posture and the binary allowlist below are unchanged: curl
+  # stays excluded so the agent cannot make raw HTTP calls with the injected
+  # token, and these entries are enforced like the rest.
+  - host: github.local
+    port: 443
+    protocol: rest
+    access: read-only
+    enforcement: enforce
+  - host: github.local
+    port: 443
+    protocol: graphql
+    access: read-only
+    enforcement: enforce
+    path: "/graphql"
 binaries:
   - "**/gh"
   - "**/node"
